    "['mpls l2vc [parameter1] [parameter2] tunnel-policy [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'xconnect 1.1.1.9 101 encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the HUAWEI `mpls l2vc` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nxconnect 1.1.1.9 101 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The Cisco command doesn't directly include the tunnel policy parameter as in HUAWEI. Tunnel selection policies would typically be configured separately in Cisco's MPLS TE configuration.\\n2. The VC ID (101) and peer address (1.1.1.9) are mapped directly to Cisco's xconnect parameters.\\n3. The `encapsulation mpls` parameter specifies the MPLS transport mechanism, equivalent to HUAWEI's L2VC implementation.\", 'trans_template': 'xconnect 1.1.1.9 101 encapsulation mpls'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls l2vpn qos cir [parameter1] pir [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'service instance 20 ethernet', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei `mpls l2vpn qos` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nservice instance 20 ethernet\\n  service policy output POLICER_NAME\\n  encapsulation dot1q 20\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, you would need to first define a policy-map with the appropriate policing values (2000 CIR/3000 PIR) and apply it to the service instance\\n2. The exact implementation might vary slightly depending on whether this is for EoMPLS or VPLS\\n3. The Cisco command doesn't have direct 1:1 parity with Huawei's simple interface-level QoS declaration, requiring separate policy-map configuration\\n\\nThe complete Cisco QoS configuration would require additional commands like:\\n```\\npolicy-map POLICER_NAME\\n  class class-default\\n    police cir 2000000 pir 3000000 conform-action transmit exceed-action drop\\n```\\n(Values converted to bps for Cisco)\", 'trans_template': 'service instance 20 ethernet'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'service policy output POLICER_NAME', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei `mpls l2vpn qos` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nservice instance 20 ethernet\\n  service policy output POLICER_NAME\\n  encapsulation dot1q 20\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, you would need to first define a policy-map with the appropriate policing values (2000 CIR/3000 PIR) and apply it to the service instance\\n2. The exact implementation might vary slightly depending on whether this is for EoMPLS or VPLS\\n3. The Cisco command doesn't have direct 1:1 parity with Huawei's simple interface-level QoS declaration, requiring separate policy-map configuration\\n\\nThe complete Cisco QoS configuration would require additional commands like:\\n```\\npolicy-map POLICER_NAME\\n  class class-default\\n    police cir 2000000 pir 3000000 conform-action transmit exceed-action drop\\n```\\n(Values converted to bps for Cisco)\", 'trans_template': 'service policy output POLICER_NAME'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation dot1q 20', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei `mpls l2vpn qos` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nservice instance 20 ethernet\\n  service policy output POLICER_NAME\\n  encapsulation dot1q 20\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, you would need to first define a policy-map with the appropriate policing values (2000 CIR/3000 PIR) and apply it to the service instance\\n2. The exact implementation might vary slightly depending on whether this is for EoMPLS or VPLS\\n3. The Cisco command doesn't have direct 1:1 parity with Huawei's simple interface-level QoS declaration, requiring separate policy-map configuration\\n\\nThe complete Cisco QoS configuration would require additional commands like:\\n```\\npolicy-map POLICER_NAME\\n  class class-default\\n    police cir 2000000 pir 3000000 conform-action transmit exceed-action drop\\n```\\n(Values converted to bps for Cisco)\", 'trans_template': 'encapsulation dot1q 20'}]]": 1,
